   "id": "uneven-income",
   "module": "02-relationships",
   "label": "Uneven income",
   "blurb": "What comes in swings from period to period against their own usual, on the figures they have shown you.",
   "kind": "risk",
   "confidence": "graded",
   "inputs": [
    "figures-on-record",
    "deal"
   ],
   "counts": [
    "money-in-by-period",
    "money-in-swing-vs-own-periods",
    "periods-covered"
   ],
   "answers": [
    "V11"
   ],
   "needs": [],
   "assumes": [],
   "assumes_status": "provisional",
   "title": "Uneven income",
   "intro": "",
   "sections": {
    "What it means": {
     "html": "<p>What this buyer takes in does not arrive evenly. Some periods are far above their own usual and some far below, on the figures they have shown you.</p>\n<p>It is a read of shape, not of size. A small steady income and a large uneven one are different answers to different questions; this one says only whether the months look alike. It describes, and does not judge the sale: <a href=\"can-they-carry-it.md\"><code>can-they-carry-it</code></a> is where an uneven income meets a fixed repayment.</p>"
    },
    "In practice": {
     "html": "<p>A lead has sent six months of statements. Money in runs close to one figure for four of them and drops to under half of it for two, which sit together. The read: \"on the six months you have, what comes in is uneven: two months well under their own usual, side by side. Six months cannot say whether that is a season. Ask for the year if it matters.\"</p>"
    },
    "How it is worked out": {
     "html": "<p>Applies the shared reading rules in <a href=\"../docs/reading-principles.md\"><code>docs/reading-principles.md</code></a>, and the rules for what is never read into a document in <a href=\"../channels/handover.md\"><code>channels/handover.md</code></a>.</p>\n<ul><li>Trigger: money in per period (counting) is set against the buyer's own median across the periods on record (counting), the own-rhythm rule applied to money. The read lands when some periods sit far from that median. The one judgement is how far counts as uneven, and it is never a fixed share of income. Where that line sits is not written yet, and the read says so rather than picking a number.</li><li>Confidence: high when many periods are on record without a gap and every figure was read from a document they handed over; softens when the periods are few, when a gap breaks the run, or when the only figure is one they said rather than showed. On fewer than twelve months it can say uneven and never seasonal, and says which.</li><li>Needs: what the buyer hands over. Without it the read has only what they said on your form or the thread, one figure with no periods to compare, so it cannot be made (a data gap, named not faked). Cash that never reaches a statement is invisible, and a figure said on an uncaptured call is a told gap until you say so.</li><li>Assumes: nothing about the shape of the sale. It stands on the buyer's own documents alone, so it holds on a lead of a fortnight as well as on a customer of years. It needs a run of periods, but that is what the documents carry, not a history with the person.</li><li>This read points neither way. It says what the figures show; whether that matters for this sale is the read above it, and what you do is yours.</li></ul>"
    }
   },
   "sectionOrder": [
    "What it means",
    "In practice",
    "How it is worked out"
   ],
   "file": "signals/uneven-income.md",
   "markdown": "---\nid: uneven-income\nmodule: 02-relationships\nlabel: Uneven income\nblurb: What comes in swings from period to period against their own usual, on the figures they have shown you.\nkind: risk\nconfidence: graded\ninputs: [figures-on-record, deal]\ncounts: [money-in-by-period, money-in-swing-vs-own-periods, periods-covered]\nanswers: [V11]\nneeds: [handover]\nassumes: []\nassumes_status: provisional\n---\n\n# Uneven income\n\n## What it means\n\nWhat this buyer takes in does not arrive evenly. Some periods are far above their own usual and\nsome far below, on the figures they have shown you.\n\nIt is a read of shape, not of size. A small steady income and a large uneven one are different\nanswers to different questions; this one says only whether the months look alike. It describes,\nand does not judge the sale: [`can-they-carry-it`](can-they-carry-it.md) is where an uneven income\nmeets a fixed repayment.\n\n## In practice\n\nA lead has sent six months of statements. Money in runs close to one figure for four of them and\ndrops to under half of it for two, which sit together. The read: \"on the six months you have, what\ncomes in is uneven: two months well under their own usual, side by side. Six months cannot say\nwhether that is a season. Ask for the year if it matters.\"\n\n## How it is worked out\n\nApplies the shared reading rules in [`docs/reading-principles.md`](../docs/reading-principles.md),\nand the rules for what is never read into a document in\n[`channels/handover.md`](../channels/handover.md).\n\n- Trigger: money in per period (counting) is set against the buyer's own median across the periods\n  on record (counting), the own-rhythm rule applied to money. The read lands when some periods sit\n  far from that median. The one judgement is how far counts as uneven, and it is never a fixed\n  share of income. Where that line sits is not written yet, and the read says so rather than\n  picking a number.\n- Confidence: high when many periods are on record without a gap and every figure was read from a\n  document they handed over; softens when the periods are few, when a gap breaks the run, or when\n  the only figure is one they said rather than showed. On fewer than twelve months it can say\n  uneven and never seasonal, and says which.\n- Needs: what the buyer hands over. Without it the read has only what they said on your form or\n  the thread, one figure with no periods to compare, so it cannot be made (a data gap, named not\n  faked). Cash that never reaches a statement is invisible, and a figure said on an uncaptured\n  call is a told gap until you say so.\n- Assumes: nothing about the shape of the sale. It stands on the buyer's own documents alone, so it\n  holds on a lead of a fortnight as well as on a customer of years. It needs a run of periods, but\n  that is what the documents carry, not a history with the person.\n- This read points neither way. It says what the figures show; whether that matters for this sale\n  is the read above it, and what you do is yours.\n",
