   "markdown": "---\nid: act-felton-director\norder: 10\nkind: act\nsignal: missing-people\nsignal_status: decided   # 22 September: worked from the records up, see ../docs/felton-pass.md. Fires on the arithmetic: nobody reached can decide, the budget holder the profile names is nobody, and Shabana is on every message\nsupporting: [champion, they-owe-you]   # new-stakeholder came off 22 September: nobody has arrived, and David is the opposite of an arrival. Champion is why the ask goes to Shabana; they-owe-you holds the two things she said she would do inside Felton, one concrete and not done, one loose\nsupporting_status: decided\ncounts: [decision-maker-reached, people-covered-vs-needed, rests-on-one-person, colleagues-looped-in-count, internal-advocacy-mentions, their-promise-undelivered]\ncounts_status: decided\nabout: [shabana-akhtar, felton]\nto: shabana-akhtar                # who the move reaches; one move per person at a time\ndocuments: []\nwidgets: [people, their-words]   # detail widgets, at most two. Each MUST resolve to ../../../widgets/*\nsure: \"a hunch\"\nsure_because: \"A reading of her words: Shabana's two mentions of David are the whole evidence that he is the one.\"\nheld_words: \"If Stephen says the budget is still the answer.\"\nreply:\n  module: buttons\nactions:\n  - label: \"Send the Ask\"\n    style: filled\n    opens: draft\n  - label: \"Not Now\"\n    says: \"Okay. I'll leave it and raise it again only if something changes.\"\n  - label: \"Not Relevant\"\n    opens: reasons\nreasons:\n  - label: \"Already Knew\"\n    says: \"Fair. I'll stop telling you things you already know about this one, and try to notice earlier next time.\"\n  - label: \"Wrong Person\"\n    says: \"Noted. I'll stop raising this person for this and look for who it should be.\"\n  - label: \"Not a Target\"\n    says: \"Understood. I'll take this off the board and not raise it again unless you put it back.\"\ndraft:\n  title: \"Draft\"\n  hand: \"Send\"\n  sub: \"in your voice · sends only when you say\"\n  footer: \"Nothing attached.\"\n---\n\n# Ask Shabana Akhtar to bring her director in\n\nStephen Walsh's objection is this year's budget, and budgets are set above him. Nobody you have reached at Felton can decide, and Shabana has named the person who can, twice.\n\n## What happened\n\n- Why next: the partial rollout offer answers the size of the number. Whether it fits this year is a priorities call, made above Stephen. Once the offer is with him, widen the room.\n- Shabana wrote \"David will want to see this\" on 15 July and \"I'll need David onside\" on 21 August. David Marshall, Director of Communities, is on no thread and has never been copied in.\n- Four people at Felton are on record and two have ever written: Shabana, who is for it and on every message, and Stephen, who holds the objection. The role your profile says holds the budget is filled by nobody. Adding the director changes the shape of the decision.\n- Shabana is the one selling this inside Felton: she brought two team leaders to the demo and finance to the thread, and said on the call it was the thing she had been trying to get them for two years. The ask goes to her because she is the one moving people.\n- Two things she said she would do inside Felton are on no record. The call with Stephen she said in July she would set up never happened; he wrote instead. \"I'll need David onside\" is a thing she means to do, not a thing she said she would do by a date, and I grade a buyer's loose words down hard. A month has passed since it and nobody new is on the thread.\n- This is a hunch more than a read. That a decider is missing is arithmetic; that David is the decider rests on her two mentions and a title on Felton's website.\n\n## People\n\n- Shabana Akhtar · Digital Lead · For it. On every message. Has mentioned her director twice\n- Stephen Walsh · Finance Business Partner · The price objection is his\n- David Marshall · Director of Communities · On no thread yet\n\n## What they said\n\n- Shabana Akhtar · 15 July · David will want to see this\n- Shabana Akhtar · 21 August · I'll need David onside\n\n## Sources\n\n- gmail · The Felton threads: Shabana's messages of 15 July and 21 August.\n- gmail · Shabana's message of 24 July: \"I'll set something up with Stephen for early August\". No invite, no event, no message saying it happened.\n- web · Felton's senior team page, David Marshall, Director of Communities.\n- gmail · The participants of every Felton thread. David is on none.\n- calendar · The June demo: Shabana, Tom Bradley and Anita Rao.\n- meet · The June demo, recorded: Shabana's own words for it.\n- goal-told · Your goal: several people to win per council, some deciders, and coalition before partial. Nobody reached at Felton decides.\n\n## Still unclear\n\n- Whether Shabana wants David in yet, or would see it as going over her head. The ask goes to her, not him.\n- Whether David is the budget holder or only the person whose services this touches. A title says what he is called.\n\n## What happens next\n\n- If Shabana agrees I'll draft the note for her to forward to David, in her voice, not yours. If she hesitates I'll drop it and wait for Stephen's reply.\n\n## The message\n\n- opens with · What Stephen said, once he has said it, and the smaller option now being with him · gmail\n- points at · Her own two mentions of David, and the session you can offer: a short note through her, or twenty minutes with them both · internal-advocacy-mentions, decision-maker-reached\n- asks · One thing: whether it would help to bring David in now. Offered as her call, in the shape she chooses · people-covered-vs-needed, goal-told\n- holds back · The call she said she would set up and did not; any reminder of it would read as a chase. And any claim about what David wants, which only she has said · their-promise-undelivered, decision-maker-reached\n\n## The draft\n\nHi Shabana,\n\nYou've mentioned David a couple of times as the person who'd need to be onside. Would it help to bring him in now that the smaller starting option is with Stephen?\n\nI'm happy to send him a short note through you, or to do a twenty-minute session with you and David. Whichever you think fits how Felton works.\n\nFede\n",
