   "markdown": "---\nid: act-neil-rhythm\norder: 13\nkind: act\nsignal: loose-end\nsignal_status: decided   # 22 September: worked from the records up, see ../docs/holbrook-pass.md. Was time-to-reconnect, which cannot fire here: he is not quieter than his usual and nothing fresh is on the web. What holds is that he asked and you promised\nsupporting: [best-way-to-reach]   # for how he takes a meeting: every one at your proposing\nsupporting_status: decided\ncounts: [their-question-unanswered, promise-made-undelivered, fulfilment-scan, reply-speed-by-channel, accepts-meetings]\ncounts_status: decided\nabout: [neil-chapman, holbrook]\nto: neil-chapman                # who the move reaches; one move per person at a time\narrives: 2026-09-16             # the day the tool puts it on the home; was the 18th, but a promise eighteen working days old is owed today\ndocuments: [east-marston-phasing-note]\nsure: \"sure\"\nsure_because: \"A fact on record: his question of 19 August, and your reply the next day promising to write it up.\"\nwhen:\n  mode: fresh\n  words: \"Worth doing today. The note has been finished since Friday.\"\nwatch:                        # what I watch for once you act; a then card arrives only if it comes\n  - for: \"Neil's reply\"\n    next: \"If he books a call, I'll prepare the phasing questions he is likely to ask.\"\nreply:\n  module: buttons\nactions:\n  - label: \"Send the Note\"\n    style: filled\n    opens: draft\n  - label: \"Not Now\"\n    says: \"Okay. I'll leave it and raise it again only if something changes.\"\n  - label: \"Not Relevant\"\n    opens: reasons\nreasons:\n  - label: \"Already Knew\"\n    says: \"Fair. I'll stop telling you things you already know about this one, and try to notice earlier next time.\"\n  - label: \"Wrong Person\"\n    says: \"Noted. I'll stop raising this person for this and look for who it should be.\"\n  - label: \"Not a Target\"\n    says: \"Understood. I'll take this off the board and not raise it again unless you put it back.\"\ndraft:\n  title: \"Draft\"\n  hand: \"Send\"\n  sub: \"in your voice · sends only when you say\"\n  footer: \"Attached: the East Marston phasing note.\"\nphone:\n  when: \"Today\"\n  act: \"Send Message\"\n  act_does: send\n  view: \"View Draft\"\n  subject: \"How East Marston did it in stages\"\n  said: \"Sent. The promise is kept, and the Holbrook invite is next.\"\n  done: \"Sent to Neil\"\n  done_text: \"The phasing note went with it, and I've marked your promise of 20 August kept. Next is the Holbrook invite, two days behind: his window closes 16 October.\"\n---\n\n# Send Neil Chapman the phasing note\n\nHe asked on 19 August how East Marston did it in stages, and you said you would write it up. The note has been finished since Friday and has not gone.\n\n## What happened\n\n- Why now: his question has sat nineteen working days, your promise eighteen, and the thing that answers both has been in Drive since 2 September, finished on the 11th, shared with nobody.\n- Since March you and Neil have had four calls, six or seven weeks apart, every one proposed by you and accepted by him. He does not chase: this is his only thread, and the only one he has opened.\n- He answers within two working days, on all four of his replies. The quiet since 20 August is about four weeks, inside his usual stretch, so this is not him going cold. It is you owing him.\n- Holbrook's window closes 16 October, in his own words. This note pays the debt and asks nothing; the invite is a separate card, two days behind it.\n\n## Sources\n\n- gmail · His message of 19 August, \"how did East Marston actually do it in stages?\", and your reply of 20 August, \"let me write up how East Marston did it and send it over\". Nothing since.\n- gmail, calendar · Your mail with Neil since March: 11 messages on 5 threads, and 4 calls, who proposed each and how fast he replies.\n- drive · The East Marston phasing note, created 2 September, finished 11 September, shared with nobody.\n- goal-told · Your goal: patient. A promise kept late is still kept; a chase is not.\n\n## Still unclear\n\n- Whether he wants the note by email or would rather talk it through. He has taken every call you proposed and proposed none.\n\n## What happens next\n\n- I'll mark the promise kept. Then the invite for the October window comes up, two days behind this. If he replies with questions I'll prepare the phasing answers from the note.\n\n## The message\n\n- opens with · The write-up he asked for on 19 August and you promised on the 20th, with the admission that it took too long · their-question-unanswered, promise-made-undelivered\n- points at · The phasing note, attached: what East Marston switched on first, what they left for later, how long each step took · east-marston-phasing-note\n- asks · Nothing. \"No need to reply.\" The ask for a meeting rests on his date and is a separate card, two days behind · chases-since-their-last-reply, goal-told\n- holds back · The October window, which is the invite's to raise and not this note's, and any date of your own · dated-facts-in-their-words\n\n## The draft\n\nHi Neil,\n\nYou asked in August how East Marston took BOPS in stages rather than all at once, and I said I would write it up. It took longer than it should have. The note is attached: what they switched on first, what they left for later, and how long each step took.\n\nNo need to reply. If it raises questions, a call whenever suits you.\n\nFede\n",
