   "markdown": "---\nid: act-north-ridley-demo-brief\norder: 2\nkind: act\nsignal: new-stakeholder\nsignal_status: decided   # 22 September: worked from the records up, see ../docs/north-ridley-pass.md. Eight names on an invite, five of them on nothing before, one of them the lead on the thing they think you replace\nsupporting: [understanding-gap, stated-priorities]   # lead-with-this came off 22 September: no use-case by kind of council has been told, so it has nothing to rank, and neither of its counts on this card could produce a figure. The angle rests on what they published and what they asked, and the opening slide on the misunderstanding\nsupporting_status: decided\ncounts: [new-attendee-on-event, prior-history-scan, head-of-signature-scan, terms-used-wrongly, priorities-they-state, how-fresh-their-words-are]\ncounts_status: decided\nabout: [michelle-turner, north-ridley]\narrives: 2026-09-16             # the day the tool puts it on the home\nheld_by: act-north-ridley-alongside\nheld_words: \"Once the note to Michelle has gone.\"\ndocuments: [east-marston-case-study, alongside-one-pager]\nsure: \"likely\"\nsure_because: \"A pattern: five of their fourteen messages ask about officer time and none about compliance, and your one recorded demo's compliance slides drew no question.\"\nwhen:\n  mode: dated\n  until: 2026-09-16\n  words: \"By this evening.\"\nreply:\n  module: buttons\nactions:\n  - label: \"Open the Brief\"\n    style: filled\n    opens: draft\n  - label: \"Not Now\"\n    says: \"Okay. I'll leave it and raise it again only if something changes.\"\n  - label: \"Not Relevant\"\n    opens: reasons\nreasons:\n  - label: \"Already Knew\"\n    says: \"Fair. I'll stop telling you things you already know about this one, and try to notice earlier next time.\"\n  - label: \"Wrong Person\"\n    says: \"Noted. I'll stop raising this person for this and look for who it should be.\"\n  - label: \"Not a Target\"\n    says: \"Understood. I'll take this off the board and not raise it again unless you put it back.\"\ndraft:\n  title: \"Brief\"\n  hand: \"Add to the Invite\"\n  sub: \"Thursday 17 September, 10:00\"\n  footer: \"Edit the brief as you like. I'll have it on your calendar entry.\"\nphone:\n  when: \"By this evening\"\n  act: \"Read the Brief\"\n  act_does: view\n  said: \"Added to the invite. Good luck tomorrow.\"\n  done: \"Brief added\"\n  done_text: \"It's in the demo invite. After the demo I'll ask how it went and what surprised you.\"\n---\n\n# Prepare Thursday's demo at North Ridley\n\nEight people, five of them new to you. Three have asked about officer time and none about compliance. Your deck opens with compliance.\n\n## What happened\n\n- Why now: the demo is tomorrow at 10:00, and the brief needs a read-through, not a rewrite, by tonight.\n- Eight invitees. Five have never been on a message, an event or a contact of yours: Nadia Frost, who leads on their case system, two of her team, Rob Fielding from ICT, and an address in Finance with no name on it. I know what they do from Michelle's message of 1 September, not from anything they wrote.\n- In 14 messages from North Ridley since July, officer time comes up five times, from three people. Compliance never. Their council plan says the same thing in their own words: give frontline officers time back, page 9, published in March.\n- Your deck, in its June and July versions, opens on \"Compliance by design\". At Felton in June, the one demo you have recorded, that section ran eighteen minutes and drew no question.\n- Open with the alongside diagram, then officer time, then East Marston's third. Keep compliance for when someone asks.\n\n## Sources\n\n- calendar · The invite for Thursday: eight names. Three of them have signatures on record; one, Nadia Frost, is on the council's own team page; four I can place only from Michelle's message.\n- gmail · Michelle's message of 1 September, naming who is coming and what each does.\n- gmail · The three North Ridley threads since July: what each person asked, and the three September messages that say migrating off or replaces.\n- web · North Ridley's council plan 2026 to 2030, page 9, published 4 March: officers' time back, in the council's words.\n- drive · Your demo deck, June and July versions, first slide \"Compliance by design\".\n- meet · The Felton demo of 16 June, recorded: the compliance slides and what they drew.\n- offering-told · The product profile, which holds no use-case by kind of council. The angle is matched by hand, from their words.\n\n## Still unclear\n\n- Who in the room decides. Michelle runs the programme and has taken this to her programme board twice; the budget holder is not on the invite, and the person from Finance has no name yet.\n\n## What happens next\n\n- After the demo I'll ask you how it went and what surprised you, then update what I know about each of the eight.\n\n## The message\n\n- opens with · The alongside diagram, because the room's word for it is \"replace\"; then officer time, which is what they published and what they asked · terms-used-wrongly, priorities-they-state\n- points at · East Marston's third, on record in the case study; the alongside one-pager; and who is in the room, by name and role · east-marston-case-study, alongside-one-pager, head-of-signature-scan\n- asks · Two things to leave with: one named officer willing to pilot, and a date to talk data residency with Rob Fielding. Of the room, not of Michelle · new-attendee-on-event, goal-told\n- holds back · Compliance, to one slide shown only if asked; any figure the case study does not state; and anything about migration, which nobody has asked you to plan · terms-used-wrongly, evidence-that-fits-them\n\n## The draft\n\n- Open with the alongside diagram. Say the word \"alongside\" in the first minute.\n- Then officer time: East Marston's case admin down by about a third. The figure three of them have asked about, five times between them.\n- In the room: Michelle Turner (programme), Nadia Frost (case system) with Ben Okafor and Hannah Price, Paul Denning and Claire Sutton (team leaders, frontline), Rob Fielding (ICT), and someone from Finance, unnamed.\n- Nadia's team will be defensive until the alongside point lands. Let her ask the first question.\n- Leave with two things: one named officer willing to pilot, and a date to talk data residency with Rob.\n- Compliance: one slide, held back, shown only if asked.\n",
