   "title": "Will you bid for the Tarlton tender?",
   "intro": "<p>Clarification questions close on Friday and the tender closes on 9 October. Whether to bid is yours: nothing I hold says what a bid would cost you against what it could win. Your answer sets what I do with Tarlton for the next fortnight.</p>",
   "sections": {
    "Known so far": {
     "html": "<ul><li>The tender asks to reduce officer time on case administration, and for a solution that works alongside existing systems. Those are your two sentences, in their words.</li><li>Two of the three things you told me a good fit looks like are met, and nothing is missed. The third, how many officers, the tender does not say, and the notice gives no value.</li><li>Tarlton is on your thirty and cold. Darren Cole in procurement is the only name, and his is not one of the three roles you said a buy needs.</li><li>Your two clarification questions went through the portal. Whatever it has answered by now is on Tarlton's page.</li></ul>"
    },
    "What's missing": {
     "html": "<ul><li>Whether you intend to bid cold. The fit says Tarlton is worth selling to. Whether the effort is worth spending is a different question, and nothing I hold answers it: not what a bid costs your side, not what this one could win.</li></ul>"
    },
    "What your answer changes": {
     "html": "<ul><li>Bid: I name a deal on Tarlton for this tender, gather what the bid needs from what we already hold, and show you the gaps.</li><li>Won't bid: I stop raising this tender and keep Tarlton on the thirty.</li><li>Not sure: I ask again on 5 October, with whatever the portal has said by then.</li></ul>"
    },
    "Where your answer is saved": {
     "html": "<ul><li>As a deal you name, on Tarlton, for the tender that closes 9 October: the record every gather about a live sale starts from. Until it exists, Tarlton has a fit and no deal.</li></ul>"
    }
   },
